{
  "description": "The rule for a utility app's back-end address (`api`), shared by the Identity Agent core (identity-agent-core/backendaddr), the login page (packages/login-web/src/app.ts, backEndAddress) and the Dart link reader (packages/login-dart, AppLink.fromFragment). `addresses` are cases of the rule itself: `accepted` says whether the address is one a back end may be named by. A case marked `dev_only` is http on this machine, which the core accepts only in a development build and which a page or Dart reader, having no build mode, accepts. `links` are cases of reading a link's api: trailing slashes are stripped and the rest must pass the rule; `read_as` is what is kept, or null when the link is refused. Hand-written, not generated: a rule changed in one place fails here in the others.",
